WEBVTT

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.423
Assalamu alaikum!

00:00:02.573 --> 00:00:08.782
This short guide shows ISSV students and parents how to join a virtual Sunday class.

00:00:09.382 --> 00:00:15.314
First, make sure you’re signed in with your LearnIslam account, not a parent’s or personal Gmail.

00:00:15.464 --> 00:00:21.268
On a shared computer, add a separate Chrome profile just for school, and use it every time.

00:00:21.868 --> 00:00:32.088
Next, go to classroom.google.com, or open the Classroom app. Your grade has two classes: one for first period, and one for second period.

00:00:32.238 --> 00:00:34.778
If you see a Join button on them, click it.

00:00:36.438 --> 00:00:45.357
On a virtual Sunday, open the class for the current period, and click Join next to Meet, at the top left. Each period has its own link.

00:00:45.957 --> 00:00:54.065
Before you join, set a school-appropriate virtual background, turn your microphone off, and keep your camera on. Then click Join now.

00:00:55.357 --> 00:00:59.817
In class, keep your camera on, and stay muted until it’s your turn to speak.

00:00:59.967 --> 00:01:02.613
To ask a question, click Raise hand.

00:01:02.763 --> 00:01:12.749
There’s no assembly on virtual days. Test your connection between 10:00 and 10:15. First period starts at 10:15, then the regular schedule.

00:01:13.349 --> 00:01:19.985
If you see Asking to join, stay on that screen. Your teacher will let you in after checking the class roster.

00:01:20.135 --> 00:01:26.920
Next time, switch to your LearnIslam account first, so you get in right away and your name matches the roster.

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:38.039
That’s it! The written steps are on the Online Classes page of the school website. Need help joining? Email issvsupport@learnislam.org.
